    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0380" n="351" xml:id="pg351"/>

                <head>71. Note From President Carter to the
                    President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs (Brzezinski)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d71-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1977-12-13">December 13, 1977</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <salute>To Zbig
                    </salute>
                </opener>
                <p>(1) Entire ExOrder is excessively verbose, repetitive &amp; confusing—even worse
                    than Ford’s 11905—Many paragraphs unnecessary—</p>
                <p>(2) Paragraph designations are impossible—3(c)(2)(iii)(A)—could be 3323(A)</p>
                <p>(3) 2(g)(3)—(p4)—Keep present arrangement of functions—Let any changes be decided
                    by a) DCI &amp; dep’t head or b) by me.</p>
                <p>(4) 3(b)(1)(iv)—(p7) I see no reason for PRC to
                    review the budget except after it is submitted by DCI to OMB. Comments to me by
                        PRC would be o.k.</p>
                <p>(5) Too much verbiage about NSC
                    SCC 3(c)—I’m not sure any of it is
                    necessary.</p>
                <p>(6) 4(b)(7)—(pp 39–40) I suggest deletion</p>
                <p>(7) 5(a)(2)(v)—(pp 46–47) Is this what we have now?</p>
                <p>(8) Keeping substance as approved by me, let Bob
                        Lipshutz help to correct problems (1) and (2) above. Expedite</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold">J.C.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
